@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Manage travel policies — Draft and simulate policy
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Corporate Administrator" as Actor
participant "Corporate Administration Workspace" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Accommodation Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events



group 1. List effective, draft, scheduled, and retired corporate policy versions.
  Actor -> Surface: List effective, draft, scheduled, and retired corporate policy versions
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/admin/policies
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: List effective, draft, scheduled, and retired corporate policy versions.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Create a new immutable draft derived from an effective version.
  Actor -> Surface: Create a new immutable draft derived from an effective version
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/admin/policies
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Create a new immutable draft derived from an effective version.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Service data
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 3. Evaluate representative scenarios without publishing the draft.
  Actor -> Surface: Evaluate representative scenarios without publishing the draft
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/admin/policies/{policyId}/preview
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Evaluate representative scenarios without publishing the draft.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Accommodation Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
